<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Operation Sapphire Fury, 2019</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P id=docs-internal-guid-50c25ec7-7fff-4d56-1e66-28d7e51157ca style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0pt; MARGIN-TOP: 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.38" dir=ltr&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-VARIANT: normal; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: #000000; FONT-STYLE: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"&gt;Several weeks ago after lengthy consultation between the Joint Chiefs and POTUS, Admiral Rolland Marshall commanding officer of USINDOPACOM received standing orders to roll back the illegal occupation of the Philippine island province of Palawan.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0pt; MARGIN-TOP: 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.38" dir=ltr&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-VARIANT: normal; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: #000000; FONT-STYLE: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"&gt;The United States had in the past stated that the growing occupation and militarization of islands in and around the South China Sea unacceptable.&amp;nbsp;Publicly stated American&amp;nbsp;policy towards the SCS littoral area was framed in the strongest words, but privately US leadership had made the decision for years to ignore what was happening &amp;nbsp;in the region. &lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0pt; MARGIN-TOP: 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.38" dir=ltr&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-VARIANT: normal; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: #000000; FONT-STYLE: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"&gt;It was perhaps this reluctance to take a greater roll that had emboldened the Chinese military to begin secretly building military facilities and air defences on the Philippine Island of Palawan, in order to finally take sea control of the SCSAO (South China Sea Area of Operations)&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0pt; MARGIN-TOP: 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.38" dir=ltr&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-VARIANT: normal; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: #000000; FONT-STYLE: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"&gt;Several weeks ago under a United Nations mandate the current President of the United States and former reality TV star made the statement&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;BR&gt;
&lt;P style="MARGIN-BOTTOM: 0pt; MARGIN-TOP: 0pt; LINE-HEIGHT: 1.38" dir=ltr&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; FONT-VARIANT: normal; VERTICAL-ALIGN: baseline; WHITE-SPACE: pre-wrap; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: #000000; FONT-STYLE: italic; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent"&gt;“What’s going on right now in the South China Sea is bad...and I mean bad on a really, really, big scale. And we will go and make things right in a way like no one has ever seen before. Just keep watching.”&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
